  "id": "COMPOUND:307 - PROTEIN:3966",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that gefitinib may interact with Receptor-type tyrosine-protein phosphatase beta through multiple indirect pathways. Gefitinib is directly linked to Ephrin type-A receptor 6, which is a target of both gefitinib and Sinocalycanchinensin G. Ephrin type-A receptor 6 is then implicated as a target of Receptor-type tyrosine-protein phosphatase beta, indicating a potential role in signaling pathways involving Ephrin receptors. Additionally, gefitinib is associated with PT-45, which is a target of staurosporine, and staurosporine is also linked to Receptor-type tyrosine-protein phosphatase beta. These findings suggest that gefitinib may modulate the activity of this receptor through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving tyrosine kinase inhibition or other signaling pathways. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between gefitinib and Receptor-type tyrosine-protein phosphatase beta, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
